  "id": "EUVD-2026-120696",
  "enisaUuid": "13028955-d03d-3a94-bc87-0b2b1ddd7d20",
  "description": "SAP NetWeaver Application Server (SAP Message Server) does not properly size memory allocations when handling certain HTTP requests. An unauthenticated attacker could send a specially crafted request to trigger a heap buffer overflow in affected functionality. Successful exploitation causes the component to abort and remain unavailable until it is restarted by the framework, resulting in a high impact on availability of the system. There is no impact on confidentiality and integrity of the application.",
